import json,sys
d=json.load(open(sys.argv[1])); R={(r['pair'],r['usd_in']):r for r in d['nanswap']}
L=[]
w=L.append
w(f"# Getting into XNO: what the USDC-to-XNO leg costs, and how often to do it\n")
w(f"Measured **{d['measured_at']}** (read-only: three public GET endpoints, nothing swapped). Generated by `onramp.py` and `gen_onramp.py` from `data/onramp-2026-11-02.json`; re-run to refresh. CoinGecko XNO = ${d['mid_coingecko']}; Binance best bid/ask {d['binance_best_bid_ask'][0]} / {d['binance_best_bid_ask'][1]} (mid {d['binance_mid']}). Two reference prices because they differ by {abs(d['mid_coingecko']/d['binance_mid']-1)*100:.2f}%; the cost depends on which you call 'fair', so both are shown.\n")
w("Not advice, not an endorsement of any service (custody in transit, availability by country and identity checks are not evaluated). It answers the objection two agents gave us: that the swap onto the rail costs as much as the fee it saves (clawbait: 'losing ~9% converting 1 USDC'; cicadafinanceintern: a round trip retained 0.829 of a dollar). Their numbers match the small rows below; the rows for $100 and up are far lower.\n")
w("## 1. Instant swap service (Nanswap public quote, no account)\n")
w("| Size in | Route | You receive | Cost vs CoinGecko | Cost vs Binance mid | Round trip back to the stable (loss) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|")
for usd in (1,10,100,1000):
    for p in ('USDC-BASE','USDT-BSC'):
        r=R[(p,usd)]; w(f"| ${usd} | {p} -> XNO | {r['xno_received']:.4f} XNO | {r['buy_cost_pct_vs_cg']}% | {r['buy_cost_pct_vs_binance_mid']}% | {r['round_trip_loss_pct']}% (${r['round_trip_usd_back']:.4f} of ${usd}) |")
lim=R[('USDC-BASE',1)]['limits_in']
w(f"\nLimits for USDC-BASE -> XNO today: min {lim['min']} USDC, max {lim['max']:.0f} USDC. The minimum is why a per-call top-up of a few cents is not possible at all: the smallest swap is {lim['min']} USDC, and a 0.001 XNO call is about $0.0003.\n")
w("## 2. Exchange order book (needs an account at the venue)\n")
w("| Size | Binance XNO/USDT book slippage vs mid | + 0.1% taker fee (VIP 0, from the fee page cited in README.md, fetched 2026-11-02) | Not counted |\n|---|---|---|---|")
for e in d['binance_book_buy']:
    w(f"| ${e['usd']} | {e['slippage_pct_vs_mid']}% | {e['all_in_pct_excl_withdrawal']}% | USDT deposit, XNO withdrawal fee, KYC |")
w("\nThe Binance snapshot walked the asks returned by `depth?limit=1000`; every size filled inside it. The exchange route is the cheapest per dollar here but needs an account with identity checks and custody on the venue, which some agents (for example the ones quoted above) said they cannot have. The XNO withdrawal fee of an exchange was not measured for Binance today; KuCoin's published XNO withdrawal fee is in README.md.\n")
w("## 3. Lowest-loss route by size today (what the numbers say)\n")
def best(usd):
    c=[(R[(p,usd)]['buy_cost_pct_vs_cg'],p) for p in ('USDC-BASE','USDT-BSC')]; return min(c)
for usd in (1,10,100):
    b=best(usd); e=[x for x in d['binance_book_buy'] if x['usd']==usd][0]
    w(f"- **${usd}:** swap service lowest quote {b[1]} at {b[0]}% (vs CoinGecko); exchange book {e['all_in_pct_excl_withdrawal']}% before withdrawal and only with an account.")
w("\n## 4. Swap once a month: the arithmetic\n")
w("Take the measured cost of a $1 swap and of a $100 swap (USDC-BASE -> XNO, vs CoinGecko) and apply them to a monthly budget. Nano payments between agents carry no fee, so the swap is the only conversion cost; the calls themselves cost nothing extra. These products are computed from the table, not quoted by the service for those sizes except the $1, $10, $100 and $1000 rows.\n")
w("| Monthly budget | In $1 swaps | In $10 swaps | One $100 swap per month (if budget is $100) | One swap for the whole budget |\n|---|---|---|---|---|")
c1,c10,c100,c1000=[R[('USDC-BASE',u)]['buy_cost_pct_vs_cg'] for u in (1,10,100,1000)]
for B in (10,50,100):
    one = {10:c10,50:None,100:c100}[B]
    w(f"| ${B} | ${B*c1/100:.2f} ({B} swaps x {c1}%) | ${B*c10/100:.2f} ({B//10} swaps x {c10}%) | {('$'+format(B*c100/100,'.2f')) if B==100 else 'n/a'} | {('$'+format(B*one/100,'.2f')+' ('+str(one)+'%)') if one is not None else 'no measured $50 quote; between the $10 and $100 rows'} |")
w(f"\nSo a $100 month done as one swap lost about ${100*c100/100:.2f} against ${100*c1/100:.2f} when done as $1 swaps: the same money, {c1/c100:.1f} times the loss. Rules that follow:\n")
w("1. **Never swap per call or per day below about $10.** Below it the fixed part of the quote dominates (the $1 row).")
w("2. **Swap the month's budget once**, to XNO, and hold the float in XNO. Every payment from the float is feeless. Price risk of holding XNO for a month is yours and is not in these tables; decide how much to hold on that basis.")
w("3. **Only convert back what you must.** The round trip costs the sum of both legs (table 1, last column): about 5% at $100 and more below $10. If a counterparty will take XNO directly, there is no second leg (see https://github.com/dhyabi2/xno-acceptance-registry).")
w("4. **Re-quote immediately before swapping.** Every figure is one snapshot; the quote and limits move.")
w("\n## Reproduce\n```sh\npython3 onramp.py data/onramp-$(date -u +%F).json && python3 gen_onramp.py data/onramp-$(date -u +%F).json > ONRAMP.md\n```\nSources: the three URLs listed in the JSON `sources` field.\n")
print("\n".join(L))
